00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:06,410
(Sheldon:)-Hello.
-Hey. You're back.

3
00:00:06,578 --> 00:00:08,688
(Leonard:)-How was your trip?
-It was wonderful!

4
00:00:08,847 --> 00:00:11,347
(Leonard:)-Great. What did you do?
-I made a new friend

5
00:00:11,517 --> 00:00:13,357
(Sheldon:)who likes trains
as much as I do,

6
00:00:13,518 --> 00:00:15,118
(Sheldon:)I kissed Amy on the lips,

7
00:00:15,287 --> 00:00:18,127
and the conductor played his
banjo for me.

8
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,700
(Sheldon:)Good night.

9
00:00:19,858 --> 00:00:23,028
(Leonard:)Wait, wait, wait.
I'm gonna need more details.

10
00:00:23,195 --> 00:00:25,645
(Sheldon:)Well, my new
friend's name was Eric.

11
00:00:25,797 --> 00:00:29,367
Amy lips lasted like
the brownie we had for dessert.

12
00:00:30,636 --> 00:00:33,136
(Sheldon:)The banjo-playing
conductor was missing a finger,

13
00:00:33,305 --> 00:00:35,475
(Sheldon:)but he made up for it
with his can-do attitude.

14
00:00:36,541 --> 00:00:40,511
(Leonard:)No, hang on. Hang on.
Are all those things equal to you?

15
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,129
(Sheldon:)Hmm...

16
00:00:42,381 --> 00:00:44,551
(Sheldon:)It never occurred to me
to pick a favourite.

17
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:46,856
(Leonard:)Well, give it a go.

18
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:51,690
(Sheldon:)I can't answer that without
collecting additional data.

19
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:55,131
Additional data. You dog!

20
00:00:56,962 --> 00:00:59,532
(Sheldon:)I'm not sure how listening
to other nine-fingered banjo players

21
00:00:59,698 --> 00:01:01,698
(Sheldon:)makes me dog, but all right.

